                                                                  5422 1451
This evaluation was performed using the reaction code TALYS       5422 1451
version 1.0. The calculations were performed with neutron, proton 5422 1451
alpha, and gamma channels open, and the following TALYS controls  5422 1451
set                                                               5422 1451
relativistic   y                                                  5422 1451
bins           50                                                 5422 1451
channels       y                                                  5422 1451
filechannels   y                                                  5422 1451
spherical      y                                                  5422 1451
localomp       n                                                  5422 1451
preequilibrium y                                                  5422 1451
twocomponent   n                                                  5422 1451
preeqmode      1                                                  5422 1451
multipreeq     n                                                  5422 1451
preeqsurface   n                                                  5422 1451
preeqcomplex   y                                                  5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
This evaluation is primarily based on the default input           5422 1451
parameters. The principal exception is that the strength of the   5422 1451
parameter Cstrip was taken to be 0.75. This controls the          5422 1451
alpha-knockout channel, which is a "pre-equilibrium" emission for 5422 1451
alpha particles. This channel affects nuclei where the alpha      5422 1451
threshold is very low, often below the incident neutron energy,   5422 1451
and lower Z. This evaluation also makes an attempt to estimate    5422 1451
the theoretical uncertainty in the calculation. This was          5422 1451
accomplished by varying most of the input parameters with a       5422 1451
Gaussian distribution with a pre-defined spread, and performing   5422 1451
100 calculations where the parameters were varied using Monte     5422 1451
Carlo sampling. Below, is a list of the input parameters          5422 1451
governing reaction dynamics, i.e., optical potential and          5422 1451
pre-equilibrium reactions, that were varied. The first entry is   5422 1451
the TALYS input control name, the second is the particle channel, 5422 1451
the third is the central value (1.000 is the TALYS default), and  5422 1451
the third is the width of the Gaussian variation. (Note that      5422 1451
M2Constant, which controls pre-equilibrium does not have a        5422 1451
particle channel identifier).                                     5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
M2constant     1.000   0.250                                      5422 1451
Cknock         a  1.000      0.2                                  5422 1451
Cstrip         a  0.750      0.25                                 5422 1451
v1adjust       n  1.000      0.005                                5422 1451
v2adjust       n  1.000      0.025                                5422 1451
v3adjust       n  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
v4adjust       n  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
w1adjust       n  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
w2adjust       n  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
d1adjust       n  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
d2adjust       n  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
d3adjust       n  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
rvadjust       n  1.000      0.002                                5422 1451
v1adjust       p  1.000      0.005                                5422 1451
v2adjust       p  1.000      0.025                                5422 1451
v3adjust       p  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
v4adjust       p  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
w1adjust       p  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
w2adjust       p  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
d1adjust       p  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
d2adjust       p  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
d3adjust       p  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
rvadjust       p  1.000      0.002                                5422 1451
v1adjust       a  1.000      0.0075                               5422 1451
v2adjust       a  1.000      0.05                                 5422 1451
v3adjust       a  1.000      0.075                                5422 1451
v4adjust       a  1.000      0.075                                5422 1451
w1adjust       a  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
w2adjust       a  1.000      0.3                                  5422 1451
d1adjust       a  1.000      0.075                                5422 1451
d2adjust       a  1.000      0.075                                5422 1451
d3adjust       a  1.000      0.075                                5422 1451
rvadjust       a  1.000      0.003                                5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
The range of the Gaussian spread was chosen to reproduce the      5422 1451
expected variation in the reaction channel, ~ 5% for neutron      5422 1451
energies > 8 MeV, and larger of the order 8-10% for lower energy  5422 1451
neutrons. Since the alpha optical potential is more uncertain,    5422 1451
generally the variation was chosen to be roughly 50% larger.      5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
The level density parameters will also varied for each nucleus in 5422 1451
the reaction chain. Here, the central values were taken to the    5422 1451
TALYS default, with a Gaussian spread of 0.02, 0.02, and 0.05 for 5422 1451
alimit, pair, and deltaW respectively. Note that this is an       5422 1451
absolute spread.                                                  5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
The evaluated cross sections were taken to be the average of the  5422 1451
Monte Carlo runs.                                                 5422 1451
                                                                  5422 1451
The resonance region was taken from ENDF/B-VII.0.                 5422 1451
